  "why": {
    "tokens": [
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "Distribution is a source of supply like purchase or production: a site set to it gets its goods from elsewhere in the company. A supplying relationship tells planning which planning cluster supplies which, item by item. Planning then covers the receiving site's shortfall with a planned distribution order, and transferring that order makes a warehouse transfer order."
      }
    ],
